{"step_index":900,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T00:07:05Z","thinking":"Initial interpretation of the user input reveals requests to \"delete missing phone numbers\" and \"delete missing data,\" along with a request to \"fill in brown.\" This resembles tasks in data validation or survey workflows. The phrasing \"missing data\" prompts a review of standard procedures for handling unavailable information in those contexts.\n\n\nAnalysis indicates the user is likely working with Excel, referencing CSV and XLSX files containing \"주황색마킹\" (orange marking). Determining the exact color representation of \"갈색\" (brown) within the Korean Excel interface is crucial for accurate data modification. The user's request, coupled with the file names, suggests an immediate need to perform data cleaning and formatting operations within the specified files.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"const fs = require('fs');\n\nfunction parseCSV(content) {\n  const rows = [];\n  let currentRow = [];\n  let currentField = '';\n  let inQuotes = false;\n  for (let i = 0; i < content.length; i++) {\n    const char = content[i];\n    const nextChar = content[i + 1];\n    if (char === '\"') {\n      if (inQuotes && nextChar === '\"') {\n        currentField += '\"';\n        i++;\n      } else {\n        inQuotes = !inQuotes;\n      }\n    } else if (char === ',' && !inQuotes) {\n      currentRow.push(currentField);\n      currentField = '';\n    } else if ((char === '\\r' || char === '\\n') && !inQuotes) {\n      if (char === '\\r' && nextChar === '\\n') i++;\n      currentRow.push(currentField);\n      if (currentRow.some(f => f.trim() !== '')) rows.push(currentRow);\n      currentRow = [];\n      currentField = '';\n    } else {\n      currentField += char;\n    }\n  }\n  if (currentField !== '' || currentRow.length > 0) {\n    currentRow.push(currentField);\n    if (currentRow.some(f => f.trim() !== '')) rows.push(currentRow);\n  }\n  return rows;\n}\n\nconst csvPath = 'C:/Users/lg/Desktop/Today/(안상숙)(STI)_(모집단현행화)_부산정보산업진흥원_2026_부산_CT산업_실태조사_260910_크레탑_배현명_최종제출본.csv';\nconst content = fs.readFileSync(csvPath, 'utf8');\nconst rows = parseCSV(content);\n\nlet noPhoneCount = 0;\nlet noBizCount = 0;\nlet noSalesCount = 0;\nlet emptyDataRows = [];\n\nrows.slice(1).forEach((r, idx) => {\n  const name = r[2];\n  const biz = r[3];\n  const phone = r[7];\n  const s24 = r[16];\n  const s25 = r[17];\n  const note = r[14];\n  const contact = r[12];\n  const closed = r[13];\n\n  if (!phone) noPhoneCount++;\n  if (!biz) noBizCount++;\n  if (!s24 && !s25) noSalesCount++;\n\n  // Rows with almost no data: no biz, no phone, no sales, no ceo, no addr...\n  const hasAddr = !!r[10];\n  const hasCeo = !!r[6];\n  if (!biz && !phone && !hasAddr && !hasCeo) {\n    emptyDataRows.push({ rowNum: idx + 2, name, cat: r[11], note });\n  }\n});\n\nconsole.log('Total rows:', rows.length - 1);\nconsole.log('No phone count:', noPhoneCount);\nconsole.log('No biz count:', noBizCount);\nconsole.log('No sales count:', noSalesCount);\nconsole.log('Rows with virtually NO data (no biz, no phone, no addr, no ceo):', emptyDataRows.length, emptyDataRows);\n","Description":"Inspect missing phone and data counts","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\lg\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\a97462f9-3976-4927-b799-281f20134eb3\\scratch\\inspect_missing_data.js","toolAction":"Write inspect_missing_data.js","toolSummary":"Write inspect_missing_data.js"}}]}
